      "title": "Medical Billing & Coding Full-Time Instructor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-10\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01a.m. CST (1:01a.m. EST) on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application progress will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Job Posting Title: Medical Billing & Coding Full-Time Instructor     Position Type: Faculty     Department: LSUE AA - Business Technology (Kristie Broussard (00056048) (Inherited))     Work Location: 0104C Health Science And Technology Building     Pay Grade: Academic     Job Description: As a full-time instructor at LSUE, this position is responsible for delivering high-quality instruction in Medical Billing and Coding and other assigned subject areas within the department. The instructor teaches courses, assists with curriculum development, and assesses student learning outcomes. The position works closely with the program coordinator and other instructors to support effective and engaging instruction. Job Responsibilities: 60% Teach assigned courses in accordance with curriculum and learning objectives; develop and update syllabi, lesson plans, course materials, and assessments; use appropriate teaching methods and technologies; provide timely, constructive feedback; and maintain accurate attendance, grade, and student records. 25% Collaborate with colleagues to develop and revise curriculum; participate in departmental and institutional meetings, committees, and professional development; remain current with advancements in the field and incorporate relevant updates into instruction; participate in professional training and development, including support for online teaching. 15% Provide academic advising and student support as needed; maintain office hours and appropriate methods of communication so students can obtain assistance and have questions addressed. Minimum Qualifications: Associate's degree Health Information Management, Health Information Technology, Medical Coding, or closely related field 2 years relevant professional experience Experience in Medical Billing and Coding - inpatient and outpatient; familiarity with revenue cycle management; Preferred Qualifications Master's Degree Health Information Management, Health Information Technology, Medical Coding, or closely related field 5 or more years of experience. Inpatient/outpatient coding, revenue cycle management, and teaching/training experience Required Certification: Must hold at least one: CCS, CCS-P, CPC, RHIA, or RHIT Job Competencies: Ability to interpret academic program requirements and provide advice-Proficient Knowledge of academic resources available to students-Proficient Knowledge of applicable computer applications and basic computer functions-Proficient Ability to provide teaching instruction-Proficient Ability to communicate effectively verbally and in writing-Proficient Knowledge of and ability to interpret and apply related University policies, procedures, principles, and practices-Proficient Knowledge of and ability to interpret and apply related University policies, procedures, principles, and practices-Proficient Salary: $36,000.00-$44,000.00     Additional Job Description: Competencies: None Special Instructions: Medical Coding & Billing Instructor     Skills Needed:     Preferred Skills:     Posting Date: September 10, 2026     Closing Date (Open Until Filled if No Date Specified):    Additional Position Information: Background Check - An offer of employment is contingent on a satisfactory pre-employment background check. Benefits - LSU offers outstanding benefits to eligible employees and their dependents including health, life, dental, and vision insurance; flexible spending accounts; retirement options; various leave options; paid holidays; wellness benefits; tuition exemption for qualified positions; training and development opportunities; employee discounts; and more!    Positions approved to work outside the State of Louisiana shall be employed through Louisiana State University’s partner, nextSource Workforce Solutions, for Employer of Record Services including but not limited to employment, benefits, payroll, and tax compliance. Positions employed through Employer of Record Services will be offered benefits and retirement as applicable through their provider and will not be eligible for State of Louisiana benefits and retirement.     Essential Position (Y/N):     LSUE is an Equal Opportunity Employer.     HCM Contact Information: Questions or concerns can be directed to the LSUE Human Resources Management Office at 337-550-1222 or emailed at hr@lsue.edu ."
